    {
      "path": "docs/javascript-typescript.md",
      "currentSha256": "ddf4fe35db11a3ff42c8c6b8f49e4c379c7b04d3eeaa765bb790ef182187def0",
      "previousSha256": "c03d59ba47a2c0177efe81235c6c75917a2b9bfc40829db54670ee639db3bc19",
      "edits": [
        {
          "start": 10738,
          "previous": "",
          "current": "For top-level `Fin n` arguments, both public JavaScript calls and direct compiled\nruntime calls reject values outside `0 <= value < n`. The\n[scalar rejection checks](evidence/npm-scalar-fin-rejection-20261007.md) cover\nNode and browser calls. A separate\n[compiled Node source-entry probe](evidence/scalar-fin-source-entry-20261008/receipt.json)\nrecords every call across six private ABIs: all 15,286 rejected calls stop before\nentering the Lean function, and 15,298 valid calls enter it. The probe uses\ninstrumented packages, including valid controls and recovery calls. Its counters\nmeasure Node execution, not browser or native-host execution.\n\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
